|~ `::absent`, the mark in a shape over a part some of the data lacks, and the
   laws declared under it.
   The rules it holds: [QSDSP#residence], [QSPTH#shape]. ~|

:absent
  |~~ An absent marks in a shape a part some of the data lacks. It marks
      a key some of the records merged there lack,
      `[{:age 30} {:age 25 :name "Bob"}] | shape` answering
      `::shape[{:age ::number :name ::absent::string}]`, and each key of the
      records an empty map stands beside, `[{:age 30} {:score 7} {}] | shape`
      answering
      `::shape[#[{:age ::absent::number} {:score ::absent::number}]]`. It
      marks the element of a vector or a set empty in some, over the shape
      of the rest and outside `::nullable`:
      `[{:labels [{:name "bug"}]} {:labels []}] | shape` answers
      `::shape[{:labels [::absent{:name ::string}]}]`.
      ::link~(::shape)
  ~~|
  ::kind
    | accepts |~~ The shape of the part where the data holds it. ~~|
    | proves :marksAKeySomeRecordsLack
        |~~ A key some records lack stands marked absent. ~~|
        ~([{:age 30} {:age 25 :name "Bob"}] | shape
          | eq ::shape[{:age ::number :name ::absent::string}])
    | proves :marksEachRecordBesideAnEmptyMap
        |~~ An empty map marks each key of the records beside it absent. ~~|
        ~([{:age 30} {:score 7} {}] | shape
          | eq ::shape[#[{:age ::absent::number} {:score ::absent::number}]])
    | proves :marksTheElementOfAVectorEmptyInSome
        |~~ The element of a vector empty in some of the data is absent. ~~|
        ~([{:labels [{:name "bug"}]} {:labels []}] | shape
          | eq ::shape[{:labels [::absent{:name ::string}]}])
    | proves :standsOutsideTheNullMark
        |~~ A key missing from some records and null in others is absent
            outside and nullable within.
        ~~|
        ~([{:age 30} {:age null} {}] | shape
          | eq ::shape[{:age ::absent::nullable::number}]);
